title: '''write-protected leaf'''
pid: 6092b77c-cf25-4f7d-867c-67ae15619898
body: |2-
  This is a write-protected viewnode
    without its body or content
    but with a containerward viewtree.
  A write-protected leaf can be decorated with view-descendents,
    e.g. (as is common) a containerward tree.
    Now it is not a leaf.
  It can also be made writable,
    which causes its content to be among its viewchildren
    if they are not already.
